.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt NQINSP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqinsp
.Nd read what a capsule says, without checking it
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fn nqinsp "const char *dir" "nqrep **rep"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqinsp
reads the seal
.Pa noqtis.sig
and the manifest
.Pa noqtis.json
of the capsule in
.Fa dir
.Pq Xr noqtis-capsule 5
with the same strict readers as
.Xr nqchk 3
(canonical JSON, the exact fields, the manifest in its canonical layout)
and stores a report in
.Fa *rep
.Pq Xr nqrep 3 .
It checks nothing else: not the manifest's SHA-256, the signature, the
timestamp or any file in the folder.
.Pp
When both parse, the report ends with rows that always pass, one per
fact:
.Bl -tag -width info.timestamp
.It Ql info.format
the manifest's format
.It Ql info.alg
the seal's algorithm
.It Ql info.key
the SHA-256 of the seal's public key, 64 lower-case hex digits
.It Ql info.created
the creation time
.It Ql info.files
the number of files listed, in decimal
.It Ql info.bytes
their total size, in decimal
.It Ql info.timestamp
.Ql present
or
.Ql none
.It Ql info.meta
the manifest's meta object as canonical JSON, only when it has one
.El
.Pp
Before them come the rows of the strict readers
.Pq Ql seal.* , Ql manifest.* , Ql path ,
as in
.Xr nqchk 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK
when the seal and the manifest parse;
.Dv NQEDEC
when one does not
.Pf ( Fa *rep
holds the failing rows);
.Dv NQEARG
for a NULL argument and
.Dv NQEMEM
when memory runs out (no report).
Free the report with
.Fn nqrepfree .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-inspect 1 ,
.Xr nqchk 3 ,
.Xr nqrep 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
